Here is a program that implements 'corewar' as described in A.K.Dewdney's 
Scientific American column of May, 1984.  I would be interested in 
collecting any battle programs anyone might develop.  

For those unfamiliar with the game , this program simulates two programs in  
a simple computer's memory, battling for survival.  The simulator alternately  
executes instructions from each until a time limit expires, or an illegal  
instruction is encountered.  Time limit implies a draw; the program with the  
illegal instruction loses.  

